The scatter plot shows the number of hours of training per week and race time (in minutes) for a group of runners.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, xscale=0.7, yscale=0.22]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(11,0);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,42);
\foreach \x in {0,2,4,6,8,10} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {6,12,18,24,30} {\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.3,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.3,0) {$0$};
\foreach \p in {(1,30),(2,28),(3,27),(4,25),(5,23),(6,22),(7,20),(8,18),(9,17),(10,15)} {\fill \p circle (2.2pt);}
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-1.8,20) {Race time (min)};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (5.5,-4.5) {Training hours/week};
\node[font=\small] at (5.5,38) {Training vs race time};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the direction of the correlation shown?

